# System Settings (DB-backed, hot-reload)

`system_settings` is a key/value DB table whose entries override the `.env` / `Config` bootstrap default at runtime. The full source of truth for each tunable's type, default, label, and validator lives in `app/settings.py` (the REGISTRY); the table only stores admin-supplied overrides.

## Files map

| Concern | File(s) |
|---|---|
| Model | [app/models.py](mdc:app/models.py) `SystemSetting` |
| Registry + load/get/set/reset/as_dict | [app/settings.py](mdc:app/settings.py) |
| Routes | [app/admin.py](mdc:app/admin.py) `settings_page`, `settings_data`, `settings_save`, `settings_reset` |
| UI | [templates/admin_settings.html](mdc:templates/admin_settings.html) |
| Bootstrap defaults | [app/config.py](mdc:app/config.py) `Config` class — these are the values returned by `reset()` |

## Precedence

```
hardcoded module literal  <  app/config.py default  <  .env  <  system_settings row
```

`app.config[key]` always holds the winning value at runtime. Consumers MUST read via `current_app.config[key]` (or `app.config[key]` inside a thread closure under `app_context`) — never re-read `os.getenv` or the `Config` class directly, or you'll miss DB overrides.

## REGISTRY structure

Each entry: `{type, default, group, label, help, validator, choices_fn?}`.

```python
_spec('DOC_THUMBNAIL_WIDTH', 'int', group='Thumbnails',
      label='Thumbnail width (px)',
      help='Render width of DOC asset first-page PNG thumbnails.',
      min=200, max=4000)
```

Types: `int`, `float`, `bool`, `string`. `min`/`max` are convenience shortcuts that build a numeric range validator. Custom validators receive the already-coerced value and may raise `ValueError`.

**`choices_fn`** (optional, `string` type only): a zero-argument callable that returns `[{'value': str, 'label': str}, ...]`. Called lazily inside `as_dict()` (always inside a Flask request context). When present, the settings UI renders a `<select>` dropdown instead of a plain text input. Used by `EXPLAIN_DEFAULT_LLM` to list enabled LLM endpoints.

